This review supersedes the interpretation in [the original incident](/kb/incidents/4471/).
The export is a snapshot from 4 October 2026, not the current support queue.

## Engineering disposition — 5 October

The [course support desk](https://hq.mega.dev/challenges/what-it-shows) reports
that #4471 closed on 5 October. The parser was **fixed** by
`fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`. The hint was **won't fix** because
the booking-v3 form was retired. These are different outcomes: closing the hint
ticket does not mean its hint was corrected.

The public follow-up tickets preserve those dispositions:
[parser — completed](https://github.com/k-dang/mega-dev-s01e03/issues/1) and
[hint — not planned](https://github.com/k-dang/mega-dev-s01e03/issues/2).
The tables below preserve the export's historical report counts and classification.

## What the evidence shows

The table below removes overlapping export rows by report ID, limits the population to
ticket #4471, and groups reports using the tenant's locale and booking form. Browser
locale and intake tags are guesses, not the cause. Counts update from the data at render time.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

### Shared parser reads day-first dates month first

The shared parser interprets dates as month/day even for tenants whose locale writes
day/month. R-41200 intended 7 April but received 4 July. R-41201 reports the reverse.
Correct parsing must use the agreed date format rather than assume month first.
Keep this cause separate from the booking-form hint defect.

### Booking-v3 prints a month-first hint for day-first tenants

Booking-v3 displays MM/DD/YYYY, so people follow a month-first instruction while the
form reads the date in the tenant's day-first order. The affected path is a form report
from a day-first tenant running booking-v3. Booking-v2's DD/MM/YYYY hint does not have
this mismatch. Correct the displayed hint to match the form's interpretation and
validate that the same entered date yields the intended calendar date.

The rendered table identifies which cause lacks its own ticket. The two GitHub issues
prepared with this review track these independent fixes and list their report IDs.

### Five one-day descriptions need follow-up

R-41202, R-41209, R-41236, R-41344 and R-41620 are flagged in desk notes. Their bodies
include one-day differences, an invite preceding its booking, and a Lisbon/Toronto
difference. These descriptions do not establish a third confirmed root cause.
The existing tenant-based classifier includes them in parser; its footnote makes that
placement visible. Retain those IDs for timezone/date-boundary investigation rather
than silently treating them as proven month/day flips or double-counting them.

## When reports arrived and when the desk merged them

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

The chart distinguishes receipt from merge time. A bulk merge is a desk action, not
evidence that all failures began that week or share one cause.

## Replace subject-only triage

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject/) is preserved as an accepted
historical record. Its subject-only rule merges unrelated failures and splits identical
failures expressed differently. It is stale according to the shared page layout's
review-age rule. A recent incident review does not make that older decision current.

[Decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause/) proposes a replacement: read the body, resolve
the tenant, compare locale and booking form, and merge only on supported shared cause.
Keep reports with unknown tenants or uncertain causes separate until investigated.

